@node Product
@chapter Product

@section Needs

@table @strong
@item Players
want to play @emph{Quake} and current community releases on modern hardware at
high frame rates, with the original look available, their own data found or
picked easily, and saves that never get corrupted.
@item Mod players
want large community maps to load within published limits, and a clear
message, not a crash, when content goes beyond them.
@item Speedrunners and demo users
want movement and timing that match the original, and demos that record and
play back.
@item The maintainer
wants a real workload that exercises current Rust GPU technology across
desktop and web, with every fidelity and performance claim backed by a test
anyone can rerun.
@item Packagers
want to build from a clean checkout on stable Rust, with no nightly compiler
and no asset download.
@end table

