@section Product principles

@enumerate
@item
@strong{Classic gameplay first, modern rendering second.} No enhancement may
change weapon timing, physics, monster decisions, trigger order, network
messages or demo playback.
@item
@strong{The server is the source of truth.} Even single player runs a server
and a client joined by the protocol-15 loopback. Renderers, audio and UI read
snapshots and never write back.
@item
@strong{Evidence over assertion.} Every fidelity, safety and speed claim names
the test that proves it, with its inputs and environment recorded.
@item
@strong{One shading source.} Lighting, palette, warp, fog and tone functions
are written once in Rust and run on the CPU and the GPU.
@item
@strong{Probe, never assume.} Every GPU feature beyond the baseline is
detected at run time, and losing the GPU falls back to software rendering.
@item
@strong{Untrusted by default.} Every byte of content and every QuakeC
instruction is checked before it is trusted.
@end enumerate

